// Generated by coax/web/changelog-page.coax from coax/CHANGELOG.md.
CC_TITLE :: "Coax changelog";
CC_SOURCE_URL :: "https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/blob/main/coax/CHANGELOG.md";
CC_LATEST :: "0.48.0";
CC_MARKDOWN :: "# Coax changelog\n\nThe compiler's recorded releases, newest first, including patch releases.\nEach commit identifies the version's introduction on `main`; explicitly labelled\nfollow-ups landed while that version was still current. Dates use the repository's\nAmerica/Chicago calendar.\n\nReconstructed from the version transitions in `src/main.cpp` (through 0.13.0)\nand [`release.coax`](release.coax) (from 0.14.0), reviewed against their changes\nand retained evidence. The initial reconstruction covers **0.37.0 to 0.1.0** through\n[`99f0d403f2b335654a54e1a60611f8c8251b3776`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/99f0d403f2b335654a54e1a60611f8c8251b3776).\nThese are compiler versions, separate from inventory, wire and protocol schema\nversions. [`STATUS.md`](STATUS.md) describes current support;\n[`RELEASE.md`](RELEASE.md) describes the release workflow.\n\n## 0.48.0 — Tagged Results and Cleanup — 2026-11-02\n\nCommit: [`1a11ccb6801a146741a7403e906489eeafb63ab1`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/1a11ccb6801a146741a7403e906489eeafb63ab1)\n\n- Add compiler-owned `Result(T,E)`, nominal tagged unions, nested `T?`\n  optionals and exhaustive selection. Keep valid active-tag construction and\n  explicit payload binding; refuse hidden Result containment in this first\n  handling profile.\n- Check direct Result obligations through transfers, branch joins, normal\n  exits and implicit propagation. Preserve left-to-right evaluation, lazy\n  fallback, assignment-place order and reverse lexical cleanup on recoverable\n  returns. Loop/defer restrictions remain explicit.\n- Track active success/error payload borrows through construction, selection,\n  propagation and checked helpers. Preserve B2's bounded raw helper-write\n  composition, its manual fallback and all existing resource limits. Mutable\n  view carriers in sums keep the same explicit manual boundary as aggregates.\n- Emit checked LP64 tagged C layouts and composed sum-capable header identities;\n  validate tags before selection/extraction. Preserve published legacy\n  inspection schemas and refuse unsupported inventories explicitly.\n- Use typed errors in a real bounded-file adapter and the WGSL tool, preserving\n  POSIX codes and one close attempt on each ordinary acquired-descriptor exit.\n  `#pure` and `#effects` remain refused until separate effect admission lands.\n- Add a generation-fenced System One owner, typed asynchronous outcomes and\n  real Lab adoption. Snapshots copy before wire reuse; stale tickets cannot\n  cancel a newer request. This is a serialized canonical-owner protocol,\n  not general linear ownership or remote exactly-once effects. Join chapters\n  6, 7, 15, 20 and 24 through the actual adapters and offline native checks.\n\n## 0.47.0 — Versioned Shader Operations — 2026-11-01\n\nCommit: [`aabbf0d5189a7b26002114733cff0de77c7d9283`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/aabbf0d5189a7b26002114733cff0de77c7d9283)\n\n- Preserve checked shader tree2 and its GPU operation registry. Emit tree3\n  when a reachable procedure uses explicit fine derivatives or helper\n  conversion; both lowerers refuse those operations under tree2.\n- Add `gpu_dpdx_fine`, `gpu_dpdy_fine`, `gpu_fwidth_fine` and\n  `gpu_demote_helper`. Generic derivatives, legacy discard and scalar CPU\n  compatibility bodies keep their meanings. Native helper conversion declares\n  its SPIR-V extension and requires the matching enabled device feature.\n- Append rich reflection2 for actual checked binding layouts, stage visibility,\n  vertex inputs, fragment outputs and derivative/control requirements. Preserve\n  the original binding report lines for trusted legacy tools.\n- Add typed array-image dimension aliases `gpu_layer_width` and\n  `gpu_layer_height` to the existing image-query operations10/11. Programs\n  using these aliases select tree3 and query an array image's three-component\n  size. Tree2 retains its existing array-query refusal.\n- Declare and reuse an implicit float vec3 for array sample coordinates when\n  the reachable source declares only vec2 and vec4. Preserve an existing\n  declared vec3 and the existing sample operations in both tree versions.\n- Follow-up 2026-11-01: a result or store holding more than 64 borrowed\n  strings no longer stops with E0381. The returned-borrow leaves (0.46) and\n  the retained-store leaves (#3696) gave every array element its own leaf,\n  so `psionic/lib/mesh/totals.coax`, whose result holds 224 strings, ran\n  past the 64-leaf budget and then past the shared work. An array whose\n  elements would not all fit the remaining 64 leaves is now one leaf, the\n  unknown element, whose origins are every element's. A record with more\n  than 64 distinct borrowed fields is still E0381.\n- Follow-up 2026-11-01: `cast(string)` borrows in the compile-time evaluator\n  too, as the spec and emitted C have it, so `coax test` and `#run` see a\n  later write through the array. Before, the evaluator copied the bytes and a\n  check could pass that the native program fails. A string frozen into a\n  constant still takes one owned snapshot, under the same live-byte and work\n  limits; a cast copies nothing.\n\n## 0.46.0 — Returned Borrow Summaries — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`9e29938427cba24fd4fa6778812c216f2f3ad1f5`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9e29938427cba24fd4fa6778812c216f2f3ad1f5)\n\n- Extend local-borrow diagnostics through resolved helper calls and aggregate return projections, preserving caller-owned descriptors and explicit manual scope for recursive/helper-store paths; qualify real caller-buffer return APIs.\n- Visit each query expression once per owner, honor `--library`, and bind\n  cached indexes to their complete payload and front-end profile/library mode.\n  Damaged or old private indexes rebuild; the public `coax.query.v1` schema\n  stays unchanged.\n- Apply each check's `#steps` during ABI2 domain preparation; insufficient\n  fuel refuses before emitting verification C.\n- Follow-up (`ax-library-check-cache`): a compile checks each loaded unit\n  once, on its own, and caches the result in `~/.cache/coax-check/` under\n  the compiler's SHA-256, the checking options and every unit in the\n  unit's closure. A unit that checks on its own is a library: its `#test`\n  and `#forall` declarations leave the consumer's input, so the consumer\n  doesn't check them again. A part that uses its loader's names, a unit\n  whose closure has an `#authority` unit or `#import_proto`, and the entry\n  file keep their checks. `--timings` reports `library_checks` (cached and\n  checked). C now holds only the generic instances that emitted code calls\n  and the print and enum-conversion helpers it uses, and the parser and\n  checker no longer touch the capacity they reserve but don't use.\n  `psionic/lib/shadow.coax --library` emits 89,083 bytes of C (was\n  140,348), and compiling the Fairy Forest page peaks at 376 MB (was 630\n  MB). The bootstrap seeds lose their unused helpers; `coax test` and\n  `coax mutate` still run every check.\n- Follow-up (#12611): a call reads a view argument for its storage when the\n  helper's result is a slice of an array in that argument's pointee, so\n  `ft(field(u))` compiles and `ft(field(a[..]))` on a local array is E0383.\n  Before, the first was E0381, which stopped the myrealm, realm, Fairy and\n  Everglade pages, and the second was accepted. A constant is one static\n  origin, and static origins that alone overflow a set collapse to one per\n  type.\n- Follow-up (`ax-library-check-cache`): `coax mutate --diagnostics json`\n  prints each surviving mutant as an `E0414` `coax.diagnostic.v1` object at\n  the mutated token, and each procedure no check reaches as `E0415` at its\n  name. The summary line stays on stdout, and the text output is unchanged.\n- Follow-up 2026-11-01: check descriptor stores in concrete bodies, including\n  void and uncalled procedures, and project helper outlives obligations at\n  actual callers. Known callee-local backing retained in caller/static\n  storage is E0383 at the original RHS or call; unknown and unsupported\n  relations remain manual. Local-carrier return composition and request\n  completion/cancellation ownership remain separate work.\n\n## 0.45.0 — Bounded Storage Library — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`1f9d64a193fcd45d08ff775fbc7f034d2ead84ba`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/1f9d64a193fcd45d08ff775fbc7f034d2ead84ba)\n\n- A generic struct's length argument may be a named integer constant as well\n  as a literal: `Box(f64, CAP)`, `Box(u8, lib.CAP)`, `CAP :: 2 * 8`. The\n  value is folded while checking, must be 1 to 1073741824 (E0357, also for a\n  non-integer or not-yet-known constant), and names the same instance as the\n  literal it equals. A name that is neither a constant nor a type is still\n  E0368.\n- `coax/lib/bounded.coax` (`coax.bounded`): `Bounded($T, $N)`, fixed-capacity\n  storage the caller owns, with `bounded_push`, `bounded_pop`, `bounded_get`,\n  `bounded_set`, `bounded_clear`, `bounded_view` and `bounded_full`. A full or\n  empty store and a slot that isn't live are refused with `false` and no\n  change. Psionic's model registry (`psionic/lib/shadow.coax`) and the fairy\n  forest's blooms (`verse/fairy-forest/forest.coax`) use it, with their\n  fixtures' outputs unchanged.\n- Programs that compiled before emit identical C.\n- Follow-up (build, `ax-build-cache`): a warm `coax/build.sh` installs the\n  cached checked build before it validates the release documents, so it no\n  longer compiles a temporary stage0 first. The bootstrap keeps each passing\n  stage0 test and mutation gate in `~/.cache/coax-gates/`, keyed by stage0's\n  inputs, the command and the gate's source closure, and reuses it on an exact\n  match. The build log prints each gate's time or `reused`.\n- Follow-up (build, `ax-release-gate`): a bootstrap mutation gate stops on\n  a surviving mutant only when it is on a line changed since a base:\n  `origin/main` for `coax/build.sh`, production's release commit for\n  `coax/web/release.sh`. Other survivors are listed in\n  `coax/bin/mutation-survivors` and `releases/<time>/MUTATION`.\n  `COAX_MUTATION_FULL=1 coax/build.sh` is the full check, which gates on\n  every survivor. A survivor also stops the build when the change removed or\n  edited a check in its file or in the file its gate mutates, and untracked\n  `.coax` files count as changed.\n- Follow-up (`ax-stale-compiler`): `coax source-digest ROOT` prints one hash\n  of the compiler sources under `ROOT/coax`, and `coax/build.sh` writes it to\n  `coax/bin/source-digest`. A failing command run from `ROOT/coax/bin/coax`\n  whose checkout's sources differ from that digest adds a note that the\n  compiler is out of date and that `ROOT/coax/build.sh` rebuilds it.\n- Follow-up (`ax-state-construction`): a `--library` unit defines, and its\n  header declares, `void coax_default_T(T *p)` for each header struct or fixed\n  array with a declared default. It writes zeros and then the defaults in\n  place, so a host's state gets the same bytes as `s: [1] T` natively. The\n  definition is weak, because every unit that uses the type defines it.\n  Browser faces call it from `coaxial_state_init` and for their globals, and\n  `coax/web/defaults.py`, which patched the generated C, is deleted. Library\n  C and headers gain only these functions; programs emit identical C.\n- Follow-up (`ax-diagnostics-json`): `--diagnostics json` prints each\n  diagnostic as one `coax.diagnostic.v1` JSON object a line on stderr, with\n  its code, severity, message, span (file, line, column, byte offset and\n  length), notes (a failing check's name and counterexample) and fixes, with\n  replacement edits for \"add 'X'\" fixes. `coax c`, `check`, `test` and\n  `mutate` take it. Without it the text output is byte-identical. `coax\n  explain` now explains E0706.\n- Follow-up (`ax-code-index`): `coax query FILE defines NAME`, `uses NAME`\n  and `exports [MODULE]` answer from the checked program through every\n  `#load`, with file, line and column, as text or with `--json` as one\n  `coax.query.v1` object. Uses include untyped constants (also where the\n  checker folded them), checks, top-level asserts and generic bodies, and\n  never a comment or a string. The index is cached in `~/.cache/coax-query/`\n  and used only while every source unit's SHA-256 matches: a warm query over\n  the compiler's sources takes under 0.1 s, a cold one about 6 s.\n- Follow-up (`ax-step-budgets`): `#steps N` after a check's name or\n  bindings gives that check its own step budget, which replaces the file's\n  in `coax test`, `#authority` compiles and `coax mutate` (a mutant never\n  gets more than its check's own budget). A check out of steps says so on\n  its `FAIL` line with its steps and budget, and its E0400 message names the\n  budget and whether it is the check's own or the file's. `coax test FILE\n  --profile steps` lists, after each check, the eight procedures that used\n  the most of its steps, with own steps, share, steps with calls and calls.\n  The Fairy Forest page's 36 checks that ran out of steps each rebuild the\n  whole world (about 114 million steps in `fairy_start`); they now carry\n  their own budgets, and all 156 of its checks pass.\n\n## 0.44.0 — Native Semantic Checks — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`d93b9cbcefc22c83c061438fc078ec23c8d0a060`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/d93b9cbcefc22c83c061438fc078ec23c8d0a060)\n\n- Qualify original checked values, guarded writes and reverse cleanup against independent expectations; add verification-only structured trap observations and bounded artifact-only seeded-defect tuple replay, without promoting failed evaluator baselines.\n\n## 0.43.0 — Generic Literal Inference — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`baca83b6844126d77059469177b16271b4a40ed7`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/baca83b6844126d77059469177b16271b4a40ed7)\n\n- A generic call binds its typed arguments first, then gives an untyped\n  literal for a bare `$T` the type they bound, or its `int`/`f64` default\n  when none did, as generic struct literals already did. `clamp(x, 0, 1)`\n  with `x: f32` now instantiates `clamp` at `f32` instead of failing with\n  E0348; a literal that cannot take the bound type is E0350 (does not fit)\n  or E0348 (non-numeric binding).\n- E0348 says the binding came \"from another argument\" (or field), since the\n  binding argument may now come later.\n- Programs that compiled before emit identical C.\n\n## 0.42.0 — Native Finite Properties — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`b9ed63a38faa74fee5557b506b2d2c042f77e4ef`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/b9ed63a38faa74fee5557b506b2d2c042f77e4ef)\n\n- Finite-domain admission, products and tuple traversal now share one Coax\n  kernel between the evaluator and native verification, preserving the\n  original bound-evaluation budgets, case order and named witnesses.\n- `coax checks-c --verification-abi 2` emits the original parameterized\n  check procedures with immutable domain metadata. ABI 1 remains the default.\n- The optional execution companion's ABI 2 mode records `execution.v2` evidence\n  from one bounded process per property, with Coax-validated shared progress.\n  Full original evaluator baselines remain mandatory; time/output exhaustion\n  and malformed or incomplete observations cannot qualify native execution.\n\n## 0.41.0 — Native Check Execution — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`b91aed93e2b4267ccdc117d6cab3f272f2a896db`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/b91aed93e2b4267ccdc117d6cab3f272f2a896db)\n\n- The optional `tools/native_check_execution.py` maintenance driver uses the\n  complete original evaluator baseline and one checked-AST C artifact at\n  checked `-O0` and `-O2`, with a fresh bounded process for each selected check.\n  `--only` scopes native execution and never filters the original baseline.\n- Coax owns baseline, bounds, source/artifact binding, EP1 framing and verdict\n  validation. Host tooling handles compilation, files, pipes, process groups\n  and compiler/SDK observations; it never lifts or rewrites check source.\n- The separate `coax.native-checks.execution.v1` record requires complete\n  matching native observations. Exhaustion, unavailable phases and malformed\n  completions cannot pass. Selected finite properties and broader trap,\n  semantic and consumer qualification remain subsequent work.\n\n\n## 0.40.0 — Generic Type Constraints — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`49e92d76ede39c1810c000f3878134243eebdcd8`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/49e92d76ede39c1810c000f3878134243eebdcd8)\n\n- A type parameter may state the built-in constraint its body needs, where it\n  is bound: `max :: (a: $T: ordered, b: $T) -> $T` or\n  `Range :: struct($T: numeric)`. `equatable` allows `==` and `!=`; `ordered`\n  adds `<` `<=` `>` `>=`; `numeric` adds `+ - * /`, compound assignment and\n  integer literals; `copyable` is assignment and passing, which every coax0\n  type allows. There is no operator overloading.\n- Generic bodies are checked against their constraints, not against each\n  instance; an unconstrained `$T` allows only assignment, passing and\n  returning. A call or instance that binds a type outside the constraint is\n  E0806 at the use, naming the declaration and the constraint; an instance\n  whose body still fails reports its errors and an instantiation trace with\n  its bindings (E0807). Unknown names are E0805 and a constraint written\n  anywhere but where the parameter is bound is E0808.\n- The parser and checker gates kill every mutant (parser 1260/1260, checker\n  5042/5042 with the constraint mutants).\n\n## 0.39.0 — Native Check Emission — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`26a9355c10e1471454f8c18b3da5cf788f70daef`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/26a9355c10e1471454f8c18b3da5cf788f70daef)\n\n- `coax checks-c FILE [--only SUBSTR] [-o checks.c]` emits verification-only\n  C11 from the compiler's checked zero-argument `#test` procedures and their\n  admitted callees. A versioned C table preserves check ordinals, byte-length\n  names and original physical locations. It emits no product `main`.\n- Coax owns eligibility, selection and closure; ordinary authority admission\n  remains mandatory. Check emission requires checked arithmetic and refuses\n  selected `#forall`, host effects and unsupported representation/lifetime\n  forms. Ordinary product C emission retains its existing behavior.\n- This is C emission, not native execution evidence. Bounded execution,\n  finite-domain properties and broader semantic/consumer qualification remain\n  separate work.\n\n## 0.38.0 — Foreign Borrowed Views — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`0b82a1587a56a4eed8ead255dd32300efe49fc30`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/0b82a1587a56a4eed8ead255dd32300efe49fc30)\n\n- `#foreign` parameters may be borrowed views of integers, floats and `bool`\n  (`[] u8`, `[] s16`, `[] f32`, `[] bool`, ...), passed as the `{data, count}`\n  struct `#export_c` uses and declared in the generated header. The host reads\n  and writes the view during the call only: no retention, ownership transfer or\n  asynchronous use; views may overlap and an empty view may have a null `data`.\n  Views of strings, structs or views, fixed arrays and view results stay E0376.\n- The entropy bridge gains `cxrand_draw(out, n)`: one call writes the caller's\n  view; `relay_conn.coax` and `cdp.coax` use it instead of n + 1 per-byte calls.\n- Same-version follow-up: `place op= value` stages the place's address when the\n  place's own indexes are sequenced through temporaries\n  (`c[a[i-1]*256+a[i]] += 1`). Spelling it twice assigned those temporaries\n  twice in one C expression, which C leaves undefined and clang rejects with\n  `-Wunsequenced`. `tests/pass/compound_view` covers it.\n\n## 0.37.0 — Generic Structs — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`6132cbaf0a0dddccbb1d3d9ae32a9659c5bf6644`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/6132cbaf0a0dddccbb1d3d9ae32a9659c5bf6644)\n\n- Generic structs: `Pair :: struct($T)` and `Box :: struct($T, $N)`, explicit\n  type applications, field-based literal deduction and generic-struct procedure\n  parameters. Concrete instances receive their own layout, defaults, evaluation\n  and C emission within the shared 256-instance budget.\n- Bindings require fixed storage; views and aggregates containing views refuse.\n- Same-version follow-ups:\n  [`3ea326018c`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/3ea326018c652ec0b099607e94adccce6073830d)\n  added selected authored Verse/Psionic plain `#test` comparisons between the\n  evaluator and checked native `-O0`/`-O2` execution. This tooling subset does\n  not qualify native `#forall` or replace authority gates.\n  [`99f0d403f2`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/99f0d403f2b335654a54e1a60611f8c8251b3776)\n  reconciled both books with delivered capabilities and added reviewed prose,\n  feature and evidence drift checks.\n- The [frozen four-task authoring corpus](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/a56793efc76411986dc48d878208f2dbaec1f767)\n  also landed under this version, with immutable oracle/start identities and\n  recorded repair, elapsed-time and edit measurements.\n\n## 0.36.0 — Array Length Parameters — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`03d153e89a947797c50330c13f48c1984fa53711`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/03d153e89a947797c50330c13f48c1984fa53711)\n\n- `$N` value parameters deduce fixed-array lengths in `[$N] T`; generic element\n  types work in `[4] $T` and `[$N] $T`.\n- Repeated bindings must agree on length; wrong argument kinds and names used\n  as both type and length parameters refuse. Corrected generated error-reference\n  headings for E06xx/E07xx.\n\n## 0.35.0 — Generic Procedure Instantiation — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`b75820e208a781453c41af45bf85ed95023e548a`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/b75820e208a781453c41af45bf85ed95023e548a)\n\n- Callable generic procedures deduce `$T` from concrete argument types and\n  borrowed-view element types. Each procedure/binding has one checked concrete\n  instance, with a 256-instance cap.\n- Instances participate in `#run`, authored checks, authority coverage, mutation\n  and native emission; timing reports include instance counts and generated\n  bytes. Constraints and value parameters were still pending.\n- Same-version follow-up:\n  [`ffdbded841`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/ffdbded84153007a41517dc50c5b6f0e0d5f221d)\n  added `coax wgsl FILE --functions`, a Coax WGSL emitter using the checked tree.\n  Web builds adopted it and removed the Python WGSL translator.\n\n## 0.34.0 — Generic Type Parameters — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`1cc85cf74f0f85aad369aee59cd151950e0f2c84`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/1cc85cf74f0f85aad369aee59cd151950e0f2c84)\n\n- `$T` procedure signatures gained lexing, parsing and placeholder type checking,\n  with explicit refusals for unbound/result-only parameters, unsupported\n  nesting, recursion, C exports and placeholder layout queries.\n- Generic calls still refused with E0397 and templates were omitted from C\n  emission. Callable instantiation arrived in 0.35.0.\n\n## 0.33.0 — Verification Evidence Records — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`6da88715c00baaf7848942c1d074e953de6df01c`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/6da88715c00baaf7848942c1d074e953de6df01c)\n\n- `coax test/mutate --evidence FILE` writes `coax.evidence.v1`, binding individual\n  checks, quantified checks, authority coverage and mutation claims to sources,\n  compiler identity, evaluator target, profile, selection and budgets.\n- Outcomes distinguish passed, counterexample, inconclusive,\n  infrastructure-error and not-checked; the worst outcome controls the verdict.\n- Same-version follow-ups added\n  [`#flat` GPU varyings](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/e9ee646abffd0eb3dc1246967cd1c8b41ec8846b),\n  [Coax DEFLATE/zlib/PNG decoding](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/8f1456e4d96af7d858acacc3ee92006f8dc3fd9a)\n  and [baseline JPEG decoding](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/b5ce59b0bada23c1cea0ca704854745823541730).\n\n## 0.32.0 — Lowering Inspection Records — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`e132ce1f3465d74e97ec3304e280e9713fd67e6a`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/e132ce1f3465d74e97ec3304e280e9713fd67e6a)\n\n- `coax deps --lowering` exposes `coax.lowering.v1`: the checked-effect ordering\n  decisions used by C emission, with declaration identities and source spans.\n- The differential reducer minimizes a seeded reversed-order lowering defect.\n  Added E0705 documentation and grammar coverage for delivered module syntax.\n- Same-version follow-up\n  [`950b375e38`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/950b375e38e9886ddf6f5cc3f329c997f578d0e2)\n  fixed SPIR-V local arrays borrowed through views to use Private storage.\n\n## 0.31.0 — Ordered Trap Evaluation — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`6d7af890ec90eed4b977b856e6de9a191670be9a`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/6d7af890ec90eed4b977b856e6de9a191670be9a)\n\n- The checked graph classifies expression effects; native C stages two trapping\n  operands and trapping destination/value evaluation in source order.\n- Qualified first-trap order at `-O0` and `-O2`, caller-visible writes,\n  exactly-once compound places and reverse cleanup for the supported subset.\n  Lowering inspection followed in 0.32.0.\n\n## 0.30.0 — Module Export Visibility — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`cbfe5dbc50530d91d4a1dd0520411815aad1bc40`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/cbfe5dbc50530d91d4a1dd0520411815aad1bc40)\n\n- `#export NAME, ...;` seals a logical module: other modules can access only its\n  listed declarations. Member source units share access while keeping their own\n  checks and authority coverage. Module inventories report exports.\n- Export lists name owned declarations only; reexports refuse. Verse HUD became\n  the first sealed production module.\n\n## 0.29.0 — Declaration Spans and Layout — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`105acc70f0abbb17d220fe36ada8c2d8ea1c5309`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/105acc70f0abbb17d220fe36ada8c2d8ea1c5309)\n\n- Dependency inventories report exact authored declaration byte ranges, lines\n  and content hashes, or generated protobuf-directive origins.\n- Added the typed `native-lp64` layout record, checked against independent C\n  size/alignment observations. `coax deps` and `coax layout` reject other target\n  names rather than implying unsupported layouts.\n\n## 0.28.0 — Qualified Module Lookup — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`e6437772c29b9554a47687fd3f78aaabf42b391d`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/e6437772c29b9554a47687fd3f78aaabf42b391d)\n\n- `#load \"FILE.coax\" as NAME;` adds module-scoped lookup and qualified types,\n  literals, procedures, constants and enum members. Ambiguity is diagnosed at\n  use; C emission qualifies private collisions and refuses incompatible public\n  symbol collisions.\n- Same-version follow-up\n  [`926cae2bfe`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/926cae2bfee9d25b6f8b8879813cef0e5cc02ea9)\n  added checked-tree SPIR-V vertex/fragment lowering for the bounded graphics\n  subset, including vectors, records, arrays, views, textures and samplers.\n\n## 0.27.0 — Module Revision Records — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`427ce9d4bed6bb2a609db728f9d283becccd4ebc`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/427ce9d4bed6bb2a609db728f9d283becccd4ebc)\n\n- `coax deps --modules` emits `coax.modules.v1`, with conservative module-content\n  and dependency revisions separate from nominal identities and source hashes.\n  These revisions do not constitute a complete cache key.\n- Shared Everglade guard types became a production module consumer.\n\n## 0.26.0 — Logical Module Identity — 2026-10-31\n\nCommit: [`9150d202ad932fc4a94254114b6d032468ba1e41`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9150d202ad932fc4a94254114b6d032468ba1e41)\n\n- `#module \"a.b\";` establishes logical ownership across loaded member units.\n  Declarations gain stable nominal `coax.decl.v1:MODULE:KIND:NAME` identities.\n- `coax deps --declarations` reports owners, identities and checked references.\n  This release established identity; lookup remained flat until 0.28.0.\n\n## 0.25.0 — Independent Compiler Profiles — 2026-10-30\n\nCommit: [`48fa03aa887cf6c30b9e4d8a28e0e50f0289d1c9`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/48fa03aa887cf6c30b9e4d8a28e0e50f0289d1c9)\n\n- Independent `--arithmetic checked|wrapping`, `--opt 0|1|2|3`,\n  `--build-profile development|release` and debug-information selections, while\n  preserving legacy defaults and `--release` behavior.\n- `--profile-report FILE` records the resolved profile; mutation receipts bind\n  it. Compile-time arithmetic and authority checks retain their existing rules.\n- Same-version follow-ups added\n  [`coax test --only`, `--list`, per-check progress and separate check-storage limits](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/03ffce741a36bb5ba5996907e8043f22ac1a3742),\n  [checked Coax scalar-to-SPIR-V emission](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/69eff0b430aad4551d35af4a6980533ab4d58ba8)\n  and [SPIR-V fill/stroke passes](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/d9804e9510a273002ce2e60a457d6fec90923744).\n- A same-version [provenance-verified compiler cache](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/6e8520ac0062dbce7e43b15c8a69e08f23f5d95c)\n  added reusable release builds, builder locking and compiler-input snapshots;\n  `COAX_BUILD_FRESH=1` retains a fresh-bootstrap path.\n\n## 0.24.0 — CUDA Warp Kernels — 2026-10-29\n\nCommit: [`3dbc6292fc7dd34237d84b142b00920ba4629a4d`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/3dbc6292fc7dd34237d84b142b00920ba4629a4d)\n\n- CUDA warp kernels: `for lane: 0..<32`, per-lane register arrays and\n  `cu_mma_bf16_16x8x16`, with a Coax CPU meaning and CUDA tensor-core lowering.\n- Same-version follow-ups added\n  [`coax metal-compute`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/c98e206bb6e00a05a62f3a8be2d3441630c6195a),\n  including the `APPLE-FF-v1` float-float profile, and\n  [bounded group kernels](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/e23facf54abddd36a4ca55bf389b6b2f76774f52)\n  with owned shared-memory writes, barriers and Apple matrix primitives.\n  General atomics remained unsupported.\n- Other same-version additions:\n  [`coax mutate --root-only`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9322269a89db5ae31cfa2ed05e869bd0f4cd350c)\n  retains all baseline checks while limiting mutation sites to the entry source;\n  [composable native headers](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/789fb4909a1a6c86cbe84b63e2d63361128f7bae)\n  share compatible ABI declarations and reject incompatible public C spellings.\n- Shared-library/tooling follow-ups added\n  [native relay/WebSocket support](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/d7373bcc825985a284f15c9d3805ee64ca00652d),\n  [TLS socket effects](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/604767080e86383ea64285ea0e83117a646f8982),\n  [JSON node parsing/writing](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/a3829b63315b090b875443422eb6b76022a48581),\n  base64, filesystem/process/argv adapters and a\n  [headless Chrome DevTools client](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/62778126aa080ca980f0015c1a608b6fd5293645).\n  The [source-unit ceiling rose from 64 to 128](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/cfe213bcfa0892aa7a7bf90c947b47af2116a4a1).\n\n## 0.23.0 — CUDA Compute Emission — 2026-10-29\n\nCommit: [`666bae043c9bd800d15ed0e7e60912fb8866fa7f`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/666bae043c9bd800d15ed0e7e60912fb8866fa7f)\n\n- `coax cuda` emits the admitted compute subset as CUDA C for NVRTC: numeric\n  views, fixed scalar arrays and reachable procedures rooted at exported\n  item kernels. Admission policy is checked Coax; refusals use E0700/E0701.\n- Psionic's BF16 projection exercised the emitted code on an RTX 4080. The\n  catalogue also recorded tested Linux x86-64/GCC host support with explicit\n  qualification limits.\n- Same-version follow-up\n  [`c5681dbb57`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/c5681dbb57a7fc2e3cd50df2c5bda1d008a7d1dc)\n  added parallel mutation workers, `--jobs`, `--shard I/N` and `--merge`, preserving\n  the serial report for the same scope.\n\n## 0.22.0 — Compiler Build Provenance — 2026-10-29\n\nCommit: [`041464193d180e49cd0e71bf9a14ff1b77d2c38a`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/041464193d180e49cd0e71bf9a14ff1b77d2c38a)\n\n- Compiler provenance records bind declared build inputs, generated artifacts,\n  toolchain/environment identity and the compiler binary. Bootstrap builds from\n  a private input snapshot; site releases verify consistency before staging.\n- Unrelated repository changes can reuse the verified compiler. The record is\n  a consistency check, not a signature or compiler-correctness proof.\n\n## 0.21.0 — Aggregate Traversal Bounds — 2026-10-29\n\nCommit: [`73c6b07d1bf8c926d51a89dd3447dc7ff63e648a`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/73c6b07d1bf8c926d51a89dd3447dc7ff63e648a)\n\n- An independent aggregate-traversal meter bounds copying, assignment, view\n  detection and initialization at 134,217,728 visits per frontend evaluation\n  or individual check, refusing with E0400.\n- Dependency/timing reports expose the limit and consumed work. Existing\n  expression-step budgets remain separate; this does not bound total process\n  memory or wall time.\n\n## 0.20.0 — Owned Interpreter Strings — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`59df8f79a361a1dde9c7d7f8448b3594895d2e81`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/59df8f79a361a1dde9c7d7f8448b3594895d2e81)\n\n- Interpreted byte-view-to-string casts use owned immutable snapshots, releasing\n  temporary owners while retaining frozen values and shared slices correctly.\n- Separate live-byte and materialization-work budgets refuse exhaustion with\n  E0400; timing reports expose owned-string peaks. Allocation failures recover\n  cleanly during freezing and default evaluation.\n\n## 0.19.0 — Conservative Mutation Scheduling — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`17c2656677d168bb4a0d037608dc425b7e531aad`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/17c2656677d168bb4a0d037608dc425b7e531aad)\n\n- Conservative mutation scheduling records baseline procedure execution and\n  runs affected isolated checks per mutant, while retaining the complete mutant\n  set and falling back to all checks for shared or unknown state.\n- `--mutation-reference`, `--mutation-stats` and `--mutation-trace` expose the\n  reference runner and scheduling evidence. Bounded evaluation failures restore\n  constant state before later checks.\n\n## 0.18.2 — Aggregate Slot Increase — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`0c7ce1d9c26aa0105e4a16b460e35cb00ad87ef0`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/0c7ce1d9c26aa0105e4a16b460e35cb00ad87ef0)\n\n- Raised the compile-time aggregate-slot ceiling from 1,048,576 to 1,572,864 to\n  admit existing Nostr JSON boundary checks. Kept the work and container limits\n  unchanged and retained boundary/refusal checks for the revised ceiling.\n\n## 0.18.1 — Iterative Aggregate Cleanup — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`d5fc7e58328986e6e16a5b62609fc181d5c439b7`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/d5fc7e58328986e6e16a5b62609fc181d5c439b7)\n\n- Iterative aggregate release prevents deep retained-view chains from exhausting\n  the host stack during cleanup.\n- Clarified that timing counters cover frontend evaluation before authority\n  checks, and documented the traversal work still outside the initial meter.\n\n## 0.18.0 — Compile Time Resource Bounds — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`bb65b83271523eaec0b015a2b5241a3d211e675a`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/bb65b83271523eaec0b015a2b5241a3d211e675a)\n\n- `--run-steps N` configures bounded shared compile-time work, with a 100,000-step\n  default and 250,000,000 maximum. Invalid inputs refuse before evaluation.\n- Independent live aggregate-slot/container limits, last-owner accounting,\n  cycle cleanup, dependency inventory fields and peak-storage timing counters.\n  These frontend limits are separate from `coax test --steps`.\n\n## 0.17.0 — Build Profile Selection — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`ed17d7cd26b591a4aa8cc2abcb50c2528ae72e37`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/ed17d7cd26b591a4aa8cc2abcb50c2528ae72e37)\n\n- `#if BUILD_DEBUG { ... } else { ... }` selects struct fields and statement\n  blocks. Both branches parse; only the selected nodes participate in checking,\n  layout, reflection, compile-time execution, authority reachability and emission.\n- The selector follows the build profile and can change native layout. General\n  conditions, conditional imports and top-level conditional declarations remained\n  unsupported.\n\n## 0.16.0 — Wide Integer Products — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`6acc1f76936b09775d83d172ef48ca968d2de72b`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/6acc1f76936b09775d83d172ef48ca968d2de72b)\n\n- `mul_wide(u64, u64)` returns the exact two-word product as\n  `CoaxU64Product.{hi, lo}`.\n- Matching checked frontend rules and compile-time evaluation, native 128-bit\n  lowering and portable wasm32 lowering, with independent arithmetic evidence.\n\n## 0.15.0 — Unsigned Modular Arithmetic — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`2c570ddb9718a3fcd51a75d1405d0e66c27e267d`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/2c570ddb9718a3fcd51a75d1405d0e66c27e267d)\n\n- Explicit `u32`/`u64` modular arithmetic: `add_wrap`, `sub_wrap` and `mul_wrap`.\n  `rotl` and `rotr` reduce the rotation count modulo the word width.\n- Matching compile-time, checked native C and wasm32 semantics preserve argument\n  order and refuse mismatched operand widths.\n\n## 0.14.0 — Canonical Release Catalogue — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`3ea7287819c37b8a0c903f249f23f99a7ce831db`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/3ea7287819c37b8a0c903f249f23f99a7ce831db)\n\n- A single checked Coax release catalogue generates CLI metadata, JSON inventory,\n  feature tables and managed book/current-version regions.\n- Compiler bootstrap, app generation and book publication refuse source,\n  snapshot or binary drift. Release, inventory-schema and historical feature\n  versions remain separate.\n\n## 0.13.0 — Native Source Debugging — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f)\n\n- Original-source native line mapping, `--debug-info`, hashed `--source-map`\n  artifacts and source-aware LLDB presentation. `--timings` reports compiler\n  phases; real engine/Metal harnesses measure native execution cost.\n- Same-version follow-ups added\n  [E0383 local-array borrow-return diagnostics](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9d0f246ba1b95ae0a491cce8e6cb15f4a1de3d21)\n  through local aliases, assignments, subranges, casts and conditionals, and\n  [fixed C lvalues for indexed places containing calls](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/e2f8432ea2c57e9fb4106fa79e44033e1f20e2fc).\n  Interprocedural and aggregate-contained lifetimes remained unchecked.\n- Further follow-ups added\n  [`value_barrier(u32|u64)`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/b9a5f216f0c0ddcf898bfb3ef0261cc4f2788be8),\n  an optimizer-opaque identity with scoped native/wasm evidence, and\n  [bounded evaluator/native differential generation and reduction](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/63c51caeaba313b07ca77fce34a91ab4291b900f).\n  The latter landed before the 0.14.0 bump, although the later catalogue records\n  its introduction as 0.14.0.\n\n## 0.12.0 — CPU Layout Reflection — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`86ec81de01f0ebf540b070f078643d7e68c45d68`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/86ec81de01f0ebf540b070f078643d7e68c45d68)\n\n- CPU layout reflection: schema-1 `type_info`, `field_info` and `enum_info`\n  produce ordinary values, with compile-time tables and bounded selectors.\n- Haunted House vertex admission consumed reflected layout. Support was scoped\n  to the bootstrap LP64 CPU layout.\n\n## 0.11.0 — Checked Source Composition — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`3837e89ed5948bc72fea70efdb713f00cdc051a4`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/3837e89ed5948bc72fea70efdb713f00cdc051a4)\n\n- Checked `#load` source graphs: canonical once-only file identity, cycle/budget\n  admission, physical-unit syntax validation and source-relative proto imports.\n- Original-file diagnostics/traps, per-file authority and private-library\n  verification. `coax deps` inventories source and descriptor inputs.\n\n## 0.10.0 — Coax Semantic Checker — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`1e0ce7636caf5a97876fca98fc02472cd6bf328c`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/1e0ce7636caf5a97876fca98fc02472cd6bf328c)\n\n- Semantic checking moved into checked Coax: names, scopes, types, layout,\n  numeric folding/range/IEEE decisions, calls, control flow, checks and Metal\n  admission.\n- Added the explicit generated checker seed, bounded indexed graph and exact\n  bootstrap regeneration. C++ remained the evaluator, emitter and storage bridge.\n\n## 0.9.0 — Coax Syntax Parser — 2026-10-28\n\nCommit: [`d7c3a1e9d3011dcd26f35c1930cf3dcb3dc3e4bd`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/d7c3a1e9d3011dcd26f35c1930cf3dcb3dc3e4bd)\n\n- Parsing and source proto-import admission moved into checked Coax: grammar,\n  precedence, diagnostics and a bounded indexed syntax tree.\n- Explicit parser bootstrap seed and fixed-point regeneration; the native\n  bridge transports tokens and reconstructs syntax-tree storage.\n\n## 0.8.0 — Coax Lexer Implementation — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`b374c75fae5d131df3e30a9324e762f27d3c04c4`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/b374c75fae5d131df3e30a9324e762f27d3c04c4)\n\n- Lexing, token recovery/diagnostics and exact decimal-to-binary64 conversion\n  moved into checked Coax.\n- Explicit generated lexer seed, authority/mutation checks and exact bootstrap\n  regeneration replaced native lexical/numeric-conversion decisions.\n\n## 0.7.1 — Coax Provenance Assembly — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`1e0e1390632653183dd4fbe6860c3bbcf2ee7bc6`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/1e0e1390632653183dd4fbe6860c3bbcf2ee7bc6)\n\n- Streaming SHA-256, hexadecimal encoding, runtime-boundary extraction and\n  importer provenance/source-envelope assembly moved into checked\n  `fingerprint.coax`; native code supplies I/O, allocation and copying.\n- Same-version follow-up\n  [`03a379cad6`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/03a379cad69dddc34732b647b9619e1f3a5b2d15)\n  guarded scalar-view typedefs so generated headers from two libraries coexist.\n\n## 0.7.0 — Coax Descriptor Importer — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`76b0837c7ca9c45ec30e1155ad3e724000dffea7`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/76b0837c7ca9c45ec30e1155ad3e724000dffea7)\n\n- Descriptor parsing, validation, option/name/dependency resolution and codec\n  generation moved into authority-checked Coax.\n- Generated C11 importer bootstrap and exact regeneration replaced the native\n  importer implementation, with no old-importer fallback.\n\n## 0.6.1 — Checked Wire Runtime — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`e190dc4ac18ba7e917b2589d7981632ea2ea6f36`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/e190dc4ac18ba7e917b2589d7981632ea2ea6f36)\n\n- Restored authoritative checked Coax wire-runtime sources, separating the pure\n  policy core from native address wrappers and gating publication on authority\n  checks and mutation.\n- Separated compatibility evidence from independent interoperability evidence;\n  fixed evaluator field access after a failed struct expression.\n\n## 0.6.0 — Native Descriptor Importer — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`9f5a2a87fcb1bc02026a089a1dd007f465f09dac`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9f5a2a87fcb1bc02026a089a1dd007f465f09dac)\n\n- Descriptor importing moved from an external Python helper into the native\n  C++20 compiler, with an embedded wire runtime and provenance fingerprints.\n  Ordinary compilation/imports became Python-free while preserving generated\n  source bytes.\n- Atomic compiler publication and an explicit Mac bootstrap target.\n\n## 0.5.1 — Verification Gate Hardening — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`c103b0852d5846ccfdb2e3270e9e6c7b3ba9836b`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/c103b0852d5846ccfdb2e3270e9e6c7b3ba9836b)\n\n- Authority coverage requires actual check-time procedure execution. Empty\n  checks/domains, uncovered procedures and no reachable mutation sites can no\n  longer silently pass.\n- Tightened equivalent-marker parsing and expanded exhaustive wire-boundary\n  checks and descriptor audit coverage.\n\n## 0.5.0 — Check First Development — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`902a131bb38017f3f96ff234984cc048807c8865`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/902a131bb38017f3f96ff234984cc048807c8865)\n\n- Check-first `#test`, finite `#forall`, `#authority`, `coax test` and\n  `coax mutate`, with bounded check budgets and counterexamples.\n- Always-on statement `#assert` and build-time authority checks.\n\n## 0.4.0 — Bounded Protobuf Codecs — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`f9e377bad6eaf13697cdbe8e5b7bdfb5d8cdb863`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/f9e377bad6eaf13697cdbe8e5b7bdfb5d8cdb863)\n\n- `#import_proto` accepts selected proto3 descriptor closures and generates\n  borrowed typed views/accessors and caller-buffer codecs, including presence,\n  oneof and repeated fields, validation and bounds checks.\n- Import-time tooling still required Python; generated runtime code did not.\n  This was the first descriptor-import release, preceding the later Coax-native\n  frontend work recorded by the current catalogue.\n\n## 0.3.0 — Aggregates and Native ABI — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`6d49ae58fc6590aaff6d3a770c6f554d741c6cd0`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/6d49ae58fc6590aaff6d3a770c6f554d741c6cd0)\n\n- Fixed-width integers/floats, untyped constants/literals, character and bit\n  operations, checked/truncating casts, defaulted structs/enums, fixed arrays\n  and borrowed views.\n- Collection loops, `break`/`continue`, `defer`, `ifx`, `size_of`, ordered operands,\n  aggregate `#run`, C exports and `lib`/`header`/`layout`/`explain`/JSON tools,\n  plus native-host demos and an expanded runnable book.\n- The [native-home branch merge](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9c0ae696832013260cae86368e0237f0c272dbf7)\n  reconciled a parallel 0.3.0 bump and added scalar `#foreign`, suffixed floats,\n  numeric conversions, math/byte intrinsics, `c --library --header` and the\n  restricted `coax metal` emitter.\n\n## 0.2.0 — Bounded Compile Time Evaluation — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`85e7706684949f54a75f9094e8a5d6a99637ec02`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/85e7706684949f54a75f9094e8a5d6a99637ec02)\n\n- Bounded scalar `#run`, compile-time `#assert`, immutable top-level constants\n  with forward references, `type_name` and `coax check`.\n- Formal bootstrap grammar and compile-time diagnostics/tests, imported from\n  aethyr-cpp revision `040329b`, retaining the missing-semicolon location fix.\n\n## 0.1.0 — Initial Compiler — 2026-10-27\n\nCommit: [`6329f3e0b3cf6fb49c0ae0686241097235f6607b`](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/6329f3e0b3cf6fb49c0ae0686241097235f6607b)\n\n- Initial compiler imported into this repository: a C++20 frontend emitting\n  self-contained C11, procedures, scalar `int`/`bool`/`string`, locals and control\n  flow.\n- Checked development arithmetic, wrapping release arithmetic, checked `print`,\n  stable diagnostics, `run`/`build`/`c`/`version`, the language specification and\n  first book chapters.\n";
CC_BLOCKS :: 338;
CC_KIND :: [CC_BLOCKS]int.[2,2,3,3,3,3,1,2,3,2,2,2,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,3,3,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,3,3,3,1,2,3,2,2,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,3,3,3,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,3,3,2,3,3,2,3,3,3,3,3,1,2,3,2,2,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,3,3,2,3,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2,2,3,1,2,3,2,2,1,2,3,2,2];
CC_TEXT :: [CC_BLOCKS]string.["The compiler's recorded releases, newest first, including patch releases. Each commit identifies the version's introduction on main; explicitly labelled follow-ups landed while that version was still current. Dates use the repository's America/Chicago calendar.","Reconstructed from the version transitions in src/main.cpp (through 0.13.0) and release.coax (from 0.14.0), reviewed against their changes and retained evidence. The initial reconstruction covers 0.37.0 to 0.1.0 through 99f0d403f2b335654a54e1a60611f8c8251b3776. These are compiler versions, separate from inventory, wire and protocol schema versions. STATUS.md describes current support; RELEASE.md describes the release workflow.","release.coax","99f0d403f2b335654a54e1a60611f8c8251b3776","STATUS.md","RELEASE.md","0.48.0 - Tagged Results and Cleanup - 2026-11-02","Commit: 1a11ccb6801a146741a7403e906489eeafb63ab1","1a11ccb6801a146741a7403e906489eeafb63ab1","- Add compiler-owned Result(T,E), nominal tagged unions, nested T? optionals and exhaustive selection. Keep valid active-tag construction and explicit payload binding; refuse hidden Result containment in this first handling profile.","- Check direct Result obligations through transfers, branch joins, normal exits and implicit propagation. Preserve left-to-right evaluation, lazy fallback, assignment-place order and reverse lexical cleanup on recoverable returns. Loop/defer restrictions remain explicit.","- Track active success/error payload borrows through construction, selection, propagation and checked helpers. Preserve B2's bounded raw helper-write composition, its manual fallback and all existing resource limits. Mutable view carriers in sums keep the same explicit manual boundary as aggregates.","- Emit checked LP64 tagged C layouts and composed sum-capable header identities; validate tags before selection/extraction. Preserve published legacy inspection schemas and refuse unsupported inventories explicitly.","- Use typed errors in a real bounded-file adapter and the WGSL tool, preserving POSIX codes and one close attempt on each ordinary acquired-descriptor exit. #pure and #effects remain refused until separate effect admission lands.","- Add a generation-fenced System One owner, typed asynchronous outcomes and real Lab adoption. Snapshots copy before wire reuse; stale tickets cannot cancel a newer request. This is a serialized canonical-owner protocol, not general linear ownership or remote exactly-once effects. Join chapters 6, 7, 15, 20 and 24 through the actual adapters and offline native checks.","0.47.0 - Versioned Shader Operations - 2026-11-01","Commit: aabbf0d5189a7b26002114733cff0de77c7d9283","aabbf0d5189a7b26002114733cff0de77c7d9283","- Preserve checked shader tree2 and its GPU operation registry. Emit tree3 when a reachable procedure uses explicit fine derivatives or helper conversion; both lowerers refuse those operations under tree2.","- Add gpu_dpdx_fine, gpu_dpdy_fine, gpu_fwidth_fine and gpu_demote_helper. Generic derivatives, legacy discard and scalar CPU compatibility bodies keep their meanings. Native helper conversion declares its SPIR-V extension and requires the matching enabled device feature.","- Append rich reflection2 for actual checked binding layouts, stage visibility, vertex inputs, fragment outputs and derivative/control requirements. Preserve the original binding report lines for trusted legacy tools.","- Add typed array-image dimension aliases gpu_layer_width and gpu_layer_height to the existing image-query operations10/11. Programs using these aliases select tree3 and query an array image's three-component size. Tree2 retains its existing array-query refusal.","- Declare and reuse an implicit float vec3 for array sample coordinates when the reachable source declares only vec2 and vec4. Preserve an existing declared vec3 and the existing sample operations in both tree versions.","- Follow-up 2026-11-01: a result or store holding more than 64 borrowed strings no longer stops with E0381. The returned-borrow leaves (0.46) and the retained-store leaves (#3696) gave every array element its own leaf, so psionic/lib/mesh/totals.coax, whose result holds 224 strings, ran past the 64-leaf budget and then past the shared work. An array whose elements would not all fit the remaining 64 leaves is now one leaf, the unknown element, whose origins are every element's. A record with more than 64 distinct borrowed fields is still E0381.","- Follow-up 2026-11-01: cast(string) borrows in the compile-time evaluator too, as the spec and emitted C have it, so coax test and #run see a later write through the array. Before, the evaluator copied the bytes and a check could pass that the native program fails. A string frozen into a constant still takes one owned snapshot, under the same live-byte and work limits; a cast copies nothing.","0.46.0 - Returned Borrow Summaries - 2026-10-31","Commit: 9e29938427cba24fd4fa6778812c216f2f3ad1f5","9e29938427cba24fd4fa6778812c216f2f3ad1f5","- Extend local-borrow diagnostics through resolved helper calls and aggregate return projections, preserving caller-owned descriptors and explicit manual scope for recursive/helper-store paths; qualify real caller-buffer return APIs.","- Visit each query expression once per owner, honor --library, and bind cached indexes to their complete payload and front-end profile/library mode. Damaged or old private indexes rebuild; the public coax.query.v1 schema stays unchanged.","- Apply each check's #steps during ABI2 domain preparation; insufficient fuel refuses before emitting verification C.","- Follow-up (ax-library-check-cache): a compile checks each loaded unit once, on its own, and caches the result in ~/.cache/coax-check/ under the compiler's SHA-256, the checking options and every unit in the unit's closure. A unit that checks on its own is a library: its #test and #forall declarations leave the consumer's input, so the consumer doesn't check them again. A part that uses its loader's names, a unit whose closure has an #authority unit or #import_proto, and the entry file keep their checks. --timings reports library_checks (cached and checked). C now holds only the generic instances that emitted code calls and the print and enum-conversion helpers it uses, and the parser and checker no longer touch the capacity they reserve but don't use. psionic/lib/shadow.coax --library emits 89,083 bytes of C (was 140,348), and compiling the Fairy Forest page peaks at 376 MB (was 630 MB). The bootstrap seeds lose their unused helpers; coax test and coax mutate still run every check.","- Follow-up (#12611): a call reads a view argument for its storage when the helper's result is a slice of an array in that argument's pointee, so ft(field(u)) compiles and ft(field(a[..])) on a local array is E0383. Before, the first was E0381, which stopped the myrealm, realm, Fairy and Everglade pages, and the second was accepted. A constant is one static origin, and static origins that alone overflow a set collapse to one per type.","- Follow-up (ax-library-check-cache): coax mutate --diagnostics json prints each surviving mutant as an E0414 coax.diagnostic.v1 object at the mutated token, and each procedure no check reaches as E0415 at its name. The summary line stays on stdout, and the text output is unchanged.","- Follow-up 2026-11-01: check descriptor stores in concrete bodies, including void and uncalled procedures, and project helper outlives obligations at actual callers. Known callee-local backing retained in caller/static storage is E0383 at the original RHS or call; unknown and unsupported relations remain manual. Local-carrier return composition and request completion/cancellation ownership remain separate work.","0.45.0 - Bounded Storage Library - 2026-10-31","Commit: 1f9d64a193fcd45d08ff775fbc7f034d2ead84ba","1f9d64a193fcd45d08ff775fbc7f034d2ead84ba","- A generic struct's length argument may be a named integer constant as well as a literal: Box(f64, CAP), Box(u8, lib.CAP), CAP :: 2 * 8. The value is folded while checking, must be 1 to 1073741824 (E0357, also for a non-integer or not-yet-known constant), and names the same instance as the literal it equals. A name that is neither a constant nor a type is still E0368.","- coax/lib/bounded.coax (coax.bounded): Bounded($T, $N), fixed-capacity storage the caller owns, with bounded_push, bounded_pop, bounded_get, bounded_set, bounded_clear, bounded_view and bounded_full. A full or empty store and a slot that isn't live are refused with false and no change. Psionic's model registry (psionic/lib/shadow.coax) and the fairy forest's blooms (verse/fairy-forest/forest.coax) use it, with their fixtures' outputs unchanged.","- Programs that compiled before emit identical C.","- Follow-up (build, ax-build-cache): a warm coax/build.sh installs the cached checked build before it validates the release documents, so it no longer compiles a temporary stage0 first. The bootstrap keeps each passing stage0 test and mutation gate in ~/.cache/coax-gates/, keyed by stage0's inputs, the command and the gate's source closure, and reuses it on an exact match. The build log prints each gate's time or reused.","- Follow-up (build, ax-release-gate): a bootstrap mutation gate stops on a surviving mutant only when it is on a line changed since a base: origin/main for coax/build.sh, production's release commit for coax/web/release.sh. Other survivors are listed in coax/bin/mutation-survivors and releases/<time>/MUTATION. COAX_MUTATION_FULL=1 coax/build.sh is the full check, which gates on every survivor. A survivor also stops the build when the change removed or edited a check in its file or in the file its gate mutates, and untracked .coax files count as changed.","- Follow-up (ax-stale-compiler): coax source-digest ROOT prints one hash of the compiler sources under ROOT/coax, and coax/build.sh writes it to coax/bin/source-digest. A failing command run from ROOT/coax/bin/coax whose checkout's sources differ from that digest adds a note that the compiler is out of date and that ROOT/coax/build.sh rebuilds it.","- Follow-up (ax-state-construction): a --library unit defines, and its header declares, void coax_default_T(T *p) for each header struct or fixed array with a declared default. It writes zeros and then the defaults in place, so a host's state gets the same bytes as s: [1] T natively. The definition is weak, because every unit that uses the type defines it. Browser faces call it from coaxial_state_init and for their globals, and coax/web/defaults.py, which patched the generated C, is deleted. Library C and headers gain only these functions; programs emit identical C.","- Follow-up (ax-diagnostics-json): --diagnostics json prints each diagnostic as one coax.diagnostic.v1 JSON object a line on stderr, with its code, severity, message, span (file, line, column, byte offset and length), notes (a failing check's name and counterexample) and fixes, with replacement edits for \"add 'X'\" fixes. coax c, check, test and mutate take it. Without it the text output is byte-identical. coax explain now explains E0706.","- Follow-up (ax-code-index): coax query FILE defines NAME, uses NAME and exports [MODULE] answer from the checked program through every #load, with file, line and column, as text or with --json as one coax.query.v1 object. Uses include untyped constants (also where the checker folded them), checks, top-level asserts and generic bodies, and never a comment or a string. The index is cached in ~/.cache/coax-query/ and used only while every source unit's SHA-256 matches: a warm query over the compiler's sources takes under 0.1 s, a cold one about 6 s.","- Follow-up (ax-step-budgets): #steps N after a check's name or bindings gives that check its own step budget, which replaces the file's in coax test, #authority compiles and coax mutate (a mutant never gets more than its check's own budget). A check out of steps says so on its FAIL line with its steps and budget, and its E0400 message names the budget and whether it is the check's own or the file's. coax test FILE --profile steps lists, after each check, the eight procedures that used the most of its steps, with own steps, share, steps with calls and calls. The Fairy Forest page's 36 checks that ran out of steps each rebuild the whole world (about 114 million steps in fairy_start); they now carry their own budgets, and all 156 of its checks pass.","0.44.0 - Native Semantic Checks - 2026-10-31","Commit: d93b9cbcefc22c83c061438fc078ec23c8d0a060","d93b9cbcefc22c83c061438fc078ec23c8d0a060","- Qualify original checked values, guarded writes and reverse cleanup against independent expectations; add verification-only structured trap observations and bounded artifact-only seeded-defect tuple replay, without promoting failed evaluator baselines.","0.43.0 - Generic Literal Inference - 2026-10-31","Commit: baca83b6844126d77059469177b16271b4a40ed7","baca83b6844126d77059469177b16271b4a40ed7","- A generic call binds its typed arguments first, then gives an untyped literal for a bare $T the type they bound, or its int/f64 default when none did, as generic struct literals already did. clamp(x, 0, 1) with x: f32 now instantiates clamp at f32 instead of failing with E0348; a literal that cannot take the bound type is E0350 (does not fit) or E0348 (non-numeric binding).","- E0348 says the binding came \"from another argument\" (or field), since the binding argument may now come later.","- Programs that compiled before emit identical C.","0.42.0 - Native Finite Properties - 2026-10-31","Commit: b9ed63a38faa74fee5557b506b2d2c042f77e4ef","b9ed63a38faa74fee5557b506b2d2c042f77e4ef","- Finite-domain admission, products and tuple traversal now share one Coax kernel between the evaluator and native verification, preserving the original bound-evaluation budgets, case order and named witnesses.","- coax checks-c --verification-abi 2 emits the original parameterized check procedures with immutable domain metadata. ABI 1 remains the default.","- The optional execution companion's ABI 2 mode records execution.v2 evidence from one bounded process per property, with Coax-validated shared progress. Full original evaluator baselines remain mandatory; time/output exhaustion and malformed or incomplete observations cannot qualify native execution.","0.41.0 - Native Check Execution - 2026-10-31","Commit: b91aed93e2b4267ccdc117d6cab3f272f2a896db","b91aed93e2b4267ccdc117d6cab3f272f2a896db","- The optional tools/native_check_execution.py maintenance driver uses the complete original evaluator baseline and one checked-AST C artifact at checked -O0 and -O2, with a fresh bounded process for each selected check. --only scopes native execution and never filters the original baseline.","- Coax owns baseline, bounds, source/artifact binding, EP1 framing and verdict validation. Host tooling handles compilation, files, pipes, process groups and compiler/SDK observations; it never lifts or rewrites check source.","- The separate coax.native-checks.execution.v1 record requires complete matching native observations. Exhaustion, unavailable phases and malformed completions cannot pass. Selected finite properties and broader trap, semantic and consumer qualification remain subsequent work.","0.40.0 - Generic Type Constraints - 2026-10-31","Commit: 49e92d76ede39c1810c000f3878134243eebdcd8","49e92d76ede39c1810c000f3878134243eebdcd8","- A type parameter may state the built-in constraint its body needs, where it is bound: max :: (a: $T: ordered, b: $T) -> $T or Range :: struct($T: numeric). equatable allows == and !=; ordered adds < <= > >=; numeric adds + - * /, compound assignment and integer literals; copyable is assignment and passing, which every coax0 type allows. There is no operator overloading.","- Generic bodies are checked against their constraints, not against each instance; an unconstrained $T allows only assignment, passing and returning. A call or instance that binds a type outside the constraint is E0806 at the use, naming the declaration and the constraint; an instance whose body still fails reports its errors and an instantiation trace with its bindings (E0807). Unknown names are E0805 and a constraint written anywhere but where the parameter is bound is E0808.","- The parser and checker gates kill every mutant (parser 1260/1260, checker 5042/5042 with the constraint mutants).","0.39.0 - Native Check Emission - 2026-10-31","Commit: 26a9355c10e1471454f8c18b3da5cf788f70daef","26a9355c10e1471454f8c18b3da5cf788f70daef","- coax checks-c FILE [--only SUBSTR] [-o checks.c] emits verification-only C11 from the compiler's checked zero-argument #test procedures and their admitted callees. A versioned C table preserves check ordinals, byte-length names and original physical locations. It emits no product main.","- Coax owns eligibility, selection and closure; ordinary authority admission remains mandatory. Check emission requires checked arithmetic and refuses selected #forall, host effects and unsupported representation/lifetime forms. Ordinary product C emission retains its existing behavior.","- This is C emission, not native execution evidence. Bounded execution, finite-domain properties and broader semantic/consumer qualification remain separate work.","0.38.0 - Foreign Borrowed Views - 2026-10-31","Commit: 0b82a1587a56a4eed8ead255dd32300efe49fc30","0b82a1587a56a4eed8ead255dd32300efe49fc30","- #foreign parameters may be borrowed views of integers, floats and bool ([] u8, [] s16, [] f32, [] bool, ...), passed as the {data, count} struct #export_c uses and declared in the generated header. The host reads and writes the view during the call only: no retention, ownership transfer or asynchronous use; views may overlap and an empty view may have a null data. Views of strings, structs or views, fixed arrays and view results stay E0376.","- The entropy bridge gains cxrand_draw(out, n): one call writes the caller's view; relay_conn.coax and cdp.coax use it instead of n + 1 per-byte calls.","- Same-version follow-up: place op= value stages the place's address when the place's own indexes are sequenced through temporaries (c[a[i-1]*256+a[i]] += 1). Spelling it twice assigned those temporaries twice in one C expression, which C leaves undefined and clang rejects with -Wunsequenced. tests/pass/compound_view covers it.","0.37.0 - Generic Structs - 2026-10-31","Commit: 6132cbaf0a0dddccbb1d3d9ae32a9659c5bf6644","6132cbaf0a0dddccbb1d3d9ae32a9659c5bf6644","- Generic structs: Pair :: struct($T) and Box :: struct($T, $N), explicit type applications, field-based literal deduction and generic-struct procedure parameters. Concrete instances receive their own layout, defaults, evaluation and C emission within the shared 256-instance budget.","- Bindings require fixed storage; views and aggregates containing views refuse.","- Same-version follow-ups: 3ea326018c added selected authored Verse/Psionic plain #test comparisons between the evaluator and checked native -O0/-O2 execution. This tooling subset does not qualify native #forall or replace authority gates. 99f0d403f2 reconciled both books with delivered capabilities and added reviewed prose, feature and evidence drift checks.","3ea326018c","99f0d403f2","- The frozen four-task authoring corpus also landed under this version, with immutable oracle/start identities and recorded repair, elapsed-time and edit measurements.","frozen four-task authoring corpus","0.36.0 - Array Length Parameters - 2026-10-31","Commit: 03d153e89a947797c50330c13f48c1984fa53711","03d153e89a947797c50330c13f48c1984fa53711","- $N value parameters deduce fixed-array lengths in [$N] T; generic element types work in [4] $T and [$N] $T.","- Repeated bindings must agree on length; wrong argument kinds and names used as both type and length parameters refuse. Corrected generated error-reference headings for E06xx/E07xx.","0.35.0 - Generic Procedure Instantiation - 2026-10-31","Commit: b75820e208a781453c41af45bf85ed95023e548a","b75820e208a781453c41af45bf85ed95023e548a","- Callable generic procedures deduce $T from concrete argument types and borrowed-view element types. Each procedure/binding has one checked concrete instance, with a 256-instance cap.","- Instances participate in #run, authored checks, authority coverage, mutation and native emission; timing reports include instance counts and generated bytes. Constraints and value parameters were still pending.","- Same-version follow-up: ffdbded841 added coax wgsl FILE --functions, a Coax WGSL emitter using the checked tree. Web builds adopted it and removed the Python WGSL translator.","ffdbded841","0.34.0 - Generic Type Parameters - 2026-10-31","Commit: 1cc85cf74f0f85aad369aee59cd151950e0f2c84","1cc85cf74f0f85aad369aee59cd151950e0f2c84","- $T procedure signatures gained lexing, parsing and placeholder type checking, with explicit refusals for unbound/result-only parameters, unsupported nesting, recursion, C exports and placeholder layout queries.","- Generic calls still refused with E0397 and templates were omitted from C emission. Callable instantiation arrived in 0.35.0.","0.33.0 - Verification Evidence Records - 2026-10-31","Commit: 6da88715c00baaf7848942c1d074e953de6df01c","6da88715c00baaf7848942c1d074e953de6df01c","- coax test/mutate --evidence FILE writes coax.evidence.v1, binding individual checks, quantified checks, authority coverage and mutation claims to sources, compiler identity, evaluator target, profile, selection and budgets.","- Outcomes distinguish passed, counterexample, inconclusive, infrastructure-error and not-checked; the worst outcome controls the verdict.","- Same-version follow-ups added #flat GPU varyings, Coax DEFLATE/zlib/PNG decoding and baseline JPEG decoding.","#flat GPU varyings","Coax DEFLATE/zlib/PNG decoding","baseline JPEG decoding","0.32.0 - Lowering Inspection Records - 2026-10-31","Commit: e132ce1f3465d74e97ec3304e280e9713fd67e6a","e132ce1f3465d74e97ec3304e280e9713fd67e6a","- coax deps --lowering exposes coax.lowering.v1: the checked-effect ordering decisions used by C emission, with declaration identities and source spans.","- The differential reducer minimizes a seeded reversed-order lowering defect. Added E0705 documentation and grammar coverage for delivered module syntax.","- Same-version follow-up 950b375e38 fixed SPIR-V local arrays borrowed through views to use Private storage.","950b375e38","0.31.0 - Ordered Trap Evaluation - 2026-10-31","Commit: 6d7af890ec90eed4b977b856e6de9a191670be9a","6d7af890ec90eed4b977b856e6de9a191670be9a","- The checked graph classifies expression effects; native C stages two trapping operands and trapping destination/value evaluation in source order.","- Qualified first-trap order at -O0 and -O2, caller-visible writes, exactly-once compound places and reverse cleanup for the supported subset. Lowering inspection followed in 0.32.0.","0.30.0 - Module Export Visibility - 2026-10-31","Commit: cbfe5dbc50530d91d4a1dd0520411815aad1bc40","cbfe5dbc50530d91d4a1dd0520411815aad1bc40","- #export NAME, ...; seals a logical module: other modules can access only its listed declarations. Member source units share access while keeping their own checks and authority coverage. Module inventories report exports.","- Export lists name owned declarations only; reexports refuse. Verse HUD became the first sealed production module.","0.29.0 - Declaration Spans and Layout - 2026-10-31","Commit: 105acc70f0abbb17d220fe36ada8c2d8ea1c5309","105acc70f0abbb17d220fe36ada8c2d8ea1c5309","- Dependency inventories report exact authored declaration byte ranges, lines and content hashes, or generated protobuf-directive origins.","- Added the typed native-lp64 layout record, checked against independent C size/alignment observations. coax deps and coax layout reject other target names rather than implying unsupported layouts.","0.28.0 - Qualified Module Lookup - 2026-10-31","Commit: e6437772c29b9554a47687fd3f78aaabf42b391d","e6437772c29b9554a47687fd3f78aaabf42b391d","- #load \"FILE.coax\" as NAME; adds module-scoped lookup and qualified types, literals, procedures, constants and enum members. Ambiguity is diagnosed at use; C emission qualifies private collisions and refuses incompatible public symbol collisions.","- Same-version follow-up 926cae2bfe added checked-tree SPIR-V vertex/fragment lowering for the bounded graphics subset, including vectors, records, arrays, views, textures and samplers.","926cae2bfe","0.27.0 - Module Revision Records - 2026-10-31","Commit: 427ce9d4bed6bb2a609db728f9d283becccd4ebc","427ce9d4bed6bb2a609db728f9d283becccd4ebc","- coax deps --modules emits coax.modules.v1, with conservative module-content and dependency revisions separate from nominal identities and source hashes. These revisions do not constitute a complete cache key.","- Shared Everglade guard types became a production module consumer.","0.26.0 - Logical Module Identity - 2026-10-31","Commit: 9150d202ad932fc4a94254114b6d032468ba1e41","9150d202ad932fc4a94254114b6d032468ba1e41","- #module \"a.b\"; establishes logical ownership across loaded member units. Declarations gain stable nominal coax.decl.v1:MODULE:KIND:NAME identities.","- coax deps --declarations reports owners, identities and checked references. This release established identity; lookup remained flat until 0.28.0.","0.25.0 - Independent Compiler Profiles - 2026-10-30","Commit: 48fa03aa887cf6c30b9e4d8a28e0e50f0289d1c9","48fa03aa887cf6c30b9e4d8a28e0e50f0289d1c9","- Independent --arithmetic checked|wrapping, --opt 0|1|2|3, --build-profile development|release and debug-information selections, while preserving legacy defaults and --release behavior.","- --profile-report FILE records the resolved profile; mutation receipts bind it. Compile-time arithmetic and authority checks retain their existing rules.","- Same-version follow-ups added coax test --only, --list, per-check progress and separate check-storage limits, checked Coax scalar-to-SPIR-V emission and SPIR-V fill/stroke passes.","coax test --only, --list, per-check progress and separate check-storage limits","checked Coax scalar-to-SPIR-V emission","SPIR-V fill/stroke passes","- A same-version provenance-verified compiler cache added reusable release builds, builder locking and compiler-input snapshots; COAX_BUILD_FRESH=1 retains a fresh-bootstrap path.","provenance-verified compiler cache","0.24.0 - CUDA Warp Kernels - 2026-10-29","Commit: 3dbc6292fc7dd34237d84b142b00920ba4629a4d","3dbc6292fc7dd34237d84b142b00920ba4629a4d","- CUDA warp kernels: for lane: 0..<32, per-lane register arrays and cu_mma_bf16_16x8x16, with a Coax CPU meaning and CUDA tensor-core lowering.","- Same-version follow-ups added coax metal-compute, including the APPLE-FF-v1 float-float profile, and bounded group kernels with owned shared-memory writes, barriers and Apple matrix primitives. General atomics remained unsupported.","coax metal-compute","bounded group kernels","- Other same-version additions: coax mutate --root-only retains all baseline checks while limiting mutation sites to the entry source; composable native headers share compatible ABI declarations and reject incompatible public C spellings.","coax mutate --root-only","composable native headers","- Shared-library/tooling follow-ups added native relay/WebSocket support, TLS socket effects, JSON node parsing/writing, base64, filesystem/process/argv adapters and a headless Chrome DevTools client. The source-unit ceiling rose from 64 to 128.","native relay/WebSocket support","TLS socket effects","JSON node parsing/writing","headless Chrome DevTools client","source-unit ceiling rose from 64 to 128","0.23.0 - CUDA Compute Emission - 2026-10-29","Commit: 666bae043c9bd800d15ed0e7e60912fb8866fa7f","666bae043c9bd800d15ed0e7e60912fb8866fa7f","- coax cuda emits the admitted compute subset as CUDA C for NVRTC: numeric views, fixed scalar arrays and reachable procedures rooted at exported item kernels. Admission policy is checked Coax; refusals use E0700/E0701.","- Psionic's BF16 projection exercised the emitted code on an RTX 4080. The catalogue also recorded tested Linux x86-64/GCC host support with explicit qualification limits.","- Same-version follow-up c5681dbb57 added parallel mutation workers, --jobs, --shard I/N and --merge, preserving the serial report for the same scope.","c5681dbb57","0.22.0 - Compiler Build Provenance - 2026-10-29","Commit: 041464193d180e49cd0e71bf9a14ff1b77d2c38a","041464193d180e49cd0e71bf9a14ff1b77d2c38a","- Compiler provenance records bind declared build inputs, generated artifacts, toolchain/environment identity and the compiler binary. Bootstrap builds from a private input snapshot; site releases verify consistency before staging.","- Unrelated repository changes can reuse the verified compiler. The record is a consistency check, not a signature or compiler-correctness proof.","0.21.0 - Aggregate Traversal Bounds - 2026-10-29","Commit: 73c6b07d1bf8c926d51a89dd3447dc7ff63e648a","73c6b07d1bf8c926d51a89dd3447dc7ff63e648a","- An independent aggregate-traversal meter bounds copying, assignment, view detection and initialization at 134,217,728 visits per frontend evaluation or individual check, refusing with E0400.","- Dependency/timing reports expose the limit and consumed work. Existing expression-step budgets remain separate; this does not bound total process memory or wall time.","0.20.0 - Owned Interpreter Strings - 2026-10-28","Commit: 59df8f79a361a1dde9c7d7f8448b3594895d2e81","59df8f79a361a1dde9c7d7f8448b3594895d2e81","- Interpreted byte-view-to-string casts use owned immutable snapshots, releasing temporary owners while retaining frozen values and shared slices correctly.","- Separate live-byte and materialization-work budgets refuse exhaustion with E0400; timing reports expose owned-string peaks. Allocation failures recover cleanly during freezing and default evaluation.","0.19.0 - Conservative Mutation Scheduling - 2026-10-28","Commit: 17c2656677d168bb4a0d037608dc425b7e531aad","17c2656677d168bb4a0d037608dc425b7e531aad","- Conservative mutation scheduling records baseline procedure execution and runs affected isolated checks per mutant, while retaining the complete mutant set and falling back to all checks for shared or unknown state.","- --mutation-reference, --mutation-stats and --mutation-trace expose the reference runner and scheduling evidence. Bounded evaluation failures restore constant state before later checks.","0.18.2 - Aggregate Slot Increase - 2026-10-28","Commit: 0c7ce1d9c26aa0105e4a16b460e35cb00ad87ef0","0c7ce1d9c26aa0105e4a16b460e35cb00ad87ef0","- Raised the compile-time aggregate-slot ceiling from 1,048,576 to 1,572,864 to admit existing Nostr JSON boundary checks. Kept the work and container limits unchanged and retained boundary/refusal checks for the revised ceiling.","0.18.1 - Iterative Aggregate Cleanup - 2026-10-28","Commit: d5fc7e58328986e6e16a5b62609fc181d5c439b7","d5fc7e58328986e6e16a5b62609fc181d5c439b7","- Iterative aggregate release prevents deep retained-view chains from exhausting the host stack during cleanup.","- Clarified that timing counters cover frontend evaluation before authority checks, and documented the traversal work still outside the initial meter.","0.18.0 - Compile Time Resource Bounds - 2026-10-28","Commit: bb65b83271523eaec0b015a2b5241a3d211e675a","bb65b83271523eaec0b015a2b5241a3d211e675a","- --run-steps N configures bounded shared compile-time work, with a 100,000-step default and 250,000,000 maximum. Invalid inputs refuse before evaluation.","- Independent live aggregate-slot/container limits, last-owner accounting, cycle cleanup, dependency inventory fields and peak-storage timing counters. These frontend limits are separate from coax test --steps.","0.17.0 - Build Profile Selection - 2026-10-28","Commit: ed17d7cd26b591a4aa8cc2abcb50c2528ae72e37","ed17d7cd26b591a4aa8cc2abcb50c2528ae72e37","- #if BUILD_DEBUG { ... } else { ... } selects struct fields and statement blocks. Both branches parse; only the selected nodes participate in checking, layout, reflection, compile-time execution, authority reachability and emission.","- The selector follows the build profile and can change native layout. General conditions, conditional imports and top-level conditional declarations remained unsupported.","0.16.0 - Wide Integer Products - 2026-10-28","Commit: 6acc1f76936b09775d83d172ef48ca968d2de72b","6acc1f76936b09775d83d172ef48ca968d2de72b","- mul_wide(u64, u64) returns the exact two-word product as CoaxU64Product.{hi, lo}.","- Matching checked frontend rules and compile-time evaluation, native 128-bit lowering and portable wasm32 lowering, with independent arithmetic evidence.","0.15.0 - Unsigned Modular Arithmetic - 2026-10-28","Commit: 2c570ddb9718a3fcd51a75d1405d0e66c27e267d","2c570ddb9718a3fcd51a75d1405d0e66c27e267d","- Explicit u32/u64 modular arithmetic: add_wrap, sub_wrap and mul_wrap. rotl and rotr reduce the rotation count modulo the word width.","- Matching compile-time, checked native C and wasm32 semantics preserve argument order and refuse mismatched operand widths.","0.14.0 - Canonical Release Catalogue - 2026-10-28","Commit: 3ea7287819c37b8a0c903f249f23f99a7ce831db","3ea7287819c37b8a0c903f249f23f99a7ce831db","- A single checked Coax release catalogue generates CLI metadata, JSON inventory, feature tables and managed book/current-version regions.","- Compiler bootstrap, app generation and book publication refuse source, snapshot or binary drift. Release, inventory-schema and historical feature versions remain separate.","0.13.0 - Native Source Debugging - 2026-10-28","Commit: 4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f","4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f","- Original-source native line mapping, --debug-info, hashed --source-map artifacts and source-aware LLDB presentation. --timings reports compiler phases; real engine/Metal harnesses measure native execution cost.","- Same-version follow-ups added E0383 local-array borrow-return diagnostics through local aliases, assignments, subranges, casts and conditionals, and fixed C lvalues for indexed places containing calls. Interprocedural and aggregate-contained lifetimes remained unchecked.","E0383 local-array borrow-return diagnostics","fixed C lvalues for indexed places containing calls","- Further follow-ups added value_barrier(u32|u64), an optimizer-opaque identity with scoped native/wasm evidence, and bounded evaluator/native differential generation and reduction. The latter landed before the 0.14.0 bump, although the later catalogue records its introduction as 0.14.0.","value_barrier(u32|u64)","bounded evaluator/native differential generation and reduction","0.12.0 - CPU Layout Reflection - 2026-10-28","Commit: 86ec81de01f0ebf540b070f078643d7e68c45d68","86ec81de01f0ebf540b070f078643d7e68c45d68","- CPU layout reflection: schema-1 type_info, field_info and enum_info produce ordinary values, with compile-time tables and bounded selectors.","- Haunted House vertex admission consumed reflected layout. Support was scoped to the bootstrap LP64 CPU layout.","0.11.0 - Checked Source Composition - 2026-10-28","Commit: 3837e89ed5948bc72fea70efdb713f00cdc051a4","3837e89ed5948bc72fea70efdb713f00cdc051a4","- Checked #load source graphs: canonical once-only file identity, cycle/budget admission, physical-unit syntax validation and source-relative proto imports.","- Original-file diagnostics/traps, per-file authority and private-library verification. coax deps inventories source and descriptor inputs.","0.10.0 - Coax Semantic Checker - 2026-10-28","Commit: 1e0ce7636caf5a97876fca98fc02472cd6bf328c","1e0ce7636caf5a97876fca98fc02472cd6bf328c","- Semantic checking moved into checked Coax: names, scopes, types, layout, numeric folding/range/IEEE decisions, calls, control flow, checks and Metal admission.","- Added the explicit generated checker seed, bounded indexed graph and exact bootstrap regeneration. C++ remained the evaluator, emitter and storage bridge.","0.9.0 - Coax Syntax Parser - 2026-10-28","Commit: d7c3a1e9d3011dcd26f35c1930cf3dcb3dc3e4bd","d7c3a1e9d3011dcd26f35c1930cf3dcb3dc3e4bd","- Parsing and source proto-import admission moved into checked Coax: grammar, precedence, diagnostics and a bounded indexed syntax tree.","- Explicit parser bootstrap seed and fixed-point regeneration; the native bridge transports tokens and reconstructs syntax-tree storage.","0.8.0 - Coax Lexer Implementation - 2026-10-27","Commit: b374c75fae5d131df3e30a9324e762f27d3c04c4","b374c75fae5d131df3e30a9324e762f27d3c04c4","- Lexing, token recovery/diagnostics and exact decimal-to-binary64 conversion moved into checked Coax.","- Explicit generated lexer seed, authority/mutation checks and exact bootstrap regeneration replaced native lexical/numeric-conversion decisions.","0.7.1 - Coax Provenance Assembly - 2026-10-27","Commit: 1e0e1390632653183dd4fbe6860c3bbcf2ee7bc6","1e0e1390632653183dd4fbe6860c3bbcf2ee7bc6","- Streaming SHA-256, hexadecimal encoding, runtime-boundary extraction and importer provenance/source-envelope assembly moved into checked fingerprint.coax; native code supplies I/O, allocation and copying.","- Same-version follow-up 03a379cad6 guarded scalar-view typedefs so generated headers from two libraries coexist.","03a379cad6","0.7.0 - Coax Descriptor Importer - 2026-10-27","Commit: 76b0837c7ca9c45ec30e1155ad3e724000dffea7","76b0837c7ca9c45ec30e1155ad3e724000dffea7","- Descriptor parsing, validation, option/name/dependency resolution and codec generation moved into authority-checked Coax.","- Generated C11 importer bootstrap and exact regeneration replaced the native importer implementation, with no old-importer fallback.","0.6.1 - Checked Wire Runtime - 2026-10-27","Commit: e190dc4ac18ba7e917b2589d7981632ea2ea6f36","e190dc4ac18ba7e917b2589d7981632ea2ea6f36","- Restored authoritative checked Coax wire-runtime sources, separating the pure policy core from native address wrappers and gating publication on authority checks and mutation.","- Separated compatibility evidence from independent interoperability evidence; fixed evaluator field access after a failed struct expression.","0.6.0 - Native Descriptor Importer - 2026-10-27","Commit: 9f5a2a87fcb1bc02026a089a1dd007f465f09dac","9f5a2a87fcb1bc02026a089a1dd007f465f09dac","- Descriptor importing moved from an external Python helper into the native C++20 compiler, with an embedded wire runtime and provenance fingerprints. Ordinary compilation/imports became Python-free while preserving generated source bytes.","- Atomic compiler publication and an explicit Mac bootstrap target.","0.5.1 - Verification Gate Hardening - 2026-10-27","Commit: c103b0852d5846ccfdb2e3270e9e6c7b3ba9836b","c103b0852d5846ccfdb2e3270e9e6c7b3ba9836b","- Authority coverage requires actual check-time procedure execution. Empty checks/domains, uncovered procedures and no reachable mutation sites can no longer silently pass.","- Tightened equivalent-marker parsing and expanded exhaustive wire-boundary checks and descriptor audit coverage.","0.5.0 - Check First Development - 2026-10-27","Commit: 902a131bb38017f3f96ff234984cc048807c8865","902a131bb38017f3f96ff234984cc048807c8865","- Check-first #test, finite #forall, #authority, coax test and coax mutate, with bounded check budgets and counterexamples.","- Always-on statement #assert and build-time authority checks.","0.4.0 - Bounded Protobuf Codecs - 2026-10-27","Commit: f9e377bad6eaf13697cdbe8e5b7bdfb5d8cdb863","f9e377bad6eaf13697cdbe8e5b7bdfb5d8cdb863","- #import_proto accepts selected proto3 descriptor closures and generates borrowed typed views/accessors and caller-buffer codecs, including presence, oneof and repeated fields, validation and bounds checks.","- Import-time tooling still required Python; generated runtime code did not. This was the first descriptor-import release, preceding the later Coax-native frontend work recorded by the current catalogue.","0.3.0 - Aggregates and Native ABI - 2026-10-27","Commit: 6d49ae58fc6590aaff6d3a770c6f554d741c6cd0","6d49ae58fc6590aaff6d3a770c6f554d741c6cd0","- Fixed-width integers/floats, untyped constants/literals, character and bit operations, checked/truncating casts, defaulted structs/enums, fixed arrays and borrowed views.","- Collection loops, break/continue, defer, ifx, size_of, ordered operands, aggregate #run, C exports and lib/header/layout/explain/JSON tools, plus native-host demos and an expanded runnable book.","- The native-home branch merge reconciled a parallel 0.3.0 bump and added scalar #foreign, suffixed floats, numeric conversions, math/byte intrinsics, c --library --header and the restricted coax metal emitter.","native-home branch merge","0.2.0 - Bounded Compile Time Evaluation - 2026-10-27","Commit: 85e7706684949f54a75f9094e8a5d6a99637ec02","85e7706684949f54a75f9094e8a5d6a99637ec02","- Bounded scalar #run, compile-time #assert, immutable top-level constants with forward references, type_name and coax check.","- Formal bootstrap grammar and compile-time diagnostics/tests, imported from aethyr-cpp revision 040329b, retaining the missing-semicolon location fix.","0.1.0 - Initial Compiler - 2026-10-27","Commit: 6329f3e0b3cf6fb49c0ae0686241097235f6607b","6329f3e0b3cf6fb49c0ae0686241097235f6607b","- Initial compiler imported into this repository: a C++20 frontend emitting self-contained C11, procedures, scalar int/bool/string, locals and control flow.","- Checked development arithmetic, wrapping release arithmetic, checked print, stable diagnostics, run/build/c/version, the language specification and first book chapters."];
